      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "If a marker locus is linked to a QTL, the difference in character values between two relatives is expected to decrease as they share more marker alleles ibd. This is the basis for the Haseman-Elston regression (1972, generalized by Amos and Elston 1989, Amos et al. 1990, Elston 1990b), which regresses the squared difference in character value between a pair of relatives on the proportion of ibd marker alleles for that pair.",
      "source_page": 527,
      "printed_page": 507,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p023:b4",
