    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "From Chapter 7, $ \\sigma(A_{1j}, A_{2j}) = \\sigma_A^2 \\cdot \\pi_{jt} $, where $ \\pi_{jt} (=0, 1/2, \\text{or } 1) $ is the proportion of alleles ibd at the QTL. (In what follows, we use the subscripts $ t $ and $ m $ to distinguish trait vs. marker loci.) Hence, the expectation of $ Y $ conditional on the proportion of QTL alleles ibd is",
