    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Dominance only causes a departure from the additive model when both QTL alleles are ibd (such as can occur with full sibs) and hence does not influence most types of relative pairs. Define the indicator variables $ f_{1,jm} $ and $ f_{2,jm} $, where $ f_{i,jm} = 1 $ if the jth pair share i marker alleles ibd, else it is zero, so that $ \\pi_{jm} = f_{2,jm} + f_{1,jm}/2 $. For full sibs, Blackwelder and Elston (1982) show that",
